The book stops at \(|f(2.6133)| = 0.0072 \approx 0.01\), but its own rule (8.3.1) for 2 decimal places is \(|f(c)| < 0.005\), and 0.0072 is not below 0.005. Three more iterations meet the rule:
9: \(c = 2.6114\), \(f(c) = -0.0260\), interval \([2.6114, 2.6133]\);
10: \(c = 2.6124\), \(f(c) = -0.0085\), interval \([2.6124, 2.6133]\);
11: \(c = 2.6129\), \(f(c) = 0.0002\), and \(0.0002 < 0.005\): stop.
The final root \(x \approx 2.61\) is unchanged.
